Z||000000||fierospeeder||06-03-2001||02:46 AM||||im in college so im living at home, but seems that i dont have any freedom still.  <BR>Thing is i dont want to leave because i will be losing my driveway with my 3 cars and my hotrod garage.  <P>It might be the girl that im dating which is causing problems.  My mother doesn't like her at all so i think thats 90% of the problem, while my sister who is still in HS seems to have more freedom then i do.  Talking to 500 guys, sleep overs getting into serious trouble...  <P>I wanted to go out at 1am but my mother had a fit that no one goes out this late, i said yah 50 years ago.  No loss to me cause my g/f is to tired to do anything.<P>Anyone else have parents that dont give you freedom or hate the person your dating?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula||06-03-2001||09:57 AM||||I live at home and go to college but I'm pretty much free what I want to do.  And if you hate the person your going out with then why are you going out with her?  Maybe you just hate that your parents dont trust you because of her.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||06-03-2001||01:03 PM||||I dont hate her, my parents do||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||06-03-2001||01:55 PM||||I lived at home thru college (graduated last year) and was free to do mostly whatever as long as I wasn't creating a lot of noise at home.  Your at the age when you should be able to go out whenever, but unfortunately if your livin under someone elses roof you have to follow their rules too.  I'd say try talking to your parents about it to see if they won't relax a bit.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||06-03-2001||02:38 PM||||I'm in college and living away from home all year long.  My family was big on the, "You can live in my house as long as you follow my rules," bit.  Well, they were much too strict for me, so I pretty much knew my entire high school years I needed to leave home after I graduated.  I moved out of the house two weeks after I graduated.<P>I agree with my parents; if you don't want to walk the line they're making you walk, then be a big boy and get your own living situation.  If you don't want to sacrifice the things you have at home, then you have to sacrifice some of your personal freedoms.  I prefer the personal freedoms, and gave up access to every tool known to man, a slot in the garage, my VW sits at home 2800 miles away, I don't see my friends but a couple times a year, and I have to live with enough stuff to fit into my car.<P>Yeah, it's nice to do whatever you feel like without worrying about what the parents say, but there's also some benefits to staying at home.  It's just what you would rather have.  If you don't think you're ready to live on your own and sacrifice what you have at home...then you'll just have to live with their rules for now.<P>I tried the, "I'm plenty responsible, never get in trouble, and nearly independent," approach with my parents, and they didn't hear a word I said.  Good luck with that.<P>Oh, and my best buddy at home has a girlfriend that his parents hate.  Both of them (him and her) have been great friends of mine, and they're both good people.  If you like the girl, and the parents don't, who cares?  If you like her enough to deal with your parent's sh1t, more power to ya!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jefrysuko||06-03-2001||05:47 PM||||Been there speeder.<P>Sometimes it is better if they don't like your girlfriend.  I moved back in to my parents house for a year after I got out of the Navy and started school.  My parents hated my g/f also and it made me look towards moving out real quick.  Now I am married and my parents love my wife.  Let me tell you that can be downright anoying.  You just can't win anything when they can get your parents against you also.  <P>My advice to you just find somewhere you can get away from everything and be left alone.  I would sudgest a country road your fiero a favorite CD and just crank the stereo  <IMG SRC="http://www.choiceradio.com/albumcovers/nocover.gif"> ||||reg||1
